  "problem": "Suppose the following random sample was drawn from the uniform distribution $U[0,1].$ \n\n$$\n0.459,\\,0.714,\\,0.938\n$$\n\nUse these numbers to generate three random numbers that follow a probability distribution with the CDF $F(x),$ given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\frac{1}{1+{e}^{-x}},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nRound your answers to $3$ decimal places.",
